Keep the drag exceptions across a settings change

The style hands the two window drag exception lists to the window
manager at the start. A change of the KDE global settings starts the
window manager again, and that call carries no list. The window manager
clears both stored sets before it reads a list. It therefore drops the
white list and the black list of the configuration file. A widget that
the file names then takes the wrong drag behaviour.

The call now carries both lists, as the call of the start does. The
drag exceptions of the file survive a settings change.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 16 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
index 63d34cc2..fae68ab8 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
@@ -4384,7 +4384,7 @@ void Style::kdeGlobalSettingsChange(int type, int)
     // }
 
     m_blurHelper->setEnabled(Utils::compositingActive());
-    m_windowManager->initialize(opts.windowDrag);
+    m_windowManager->initialize(opts.windowDrag, opts.windowDragWhiteList.values(), opts.windowDragBlackList.values());
 }
 
 void Style::borderSizesChanged()
